{"ref":"relic:green-eyes-vizard","lead":[{"k":"p","c":["Green Eyes Vizard is a relic located in ",{"t":"The Lycaeum","r":"stage:the-lycaeum"},". Once collected, it allows ",{"i":"Sprite-Bat_Dragon.png","w":24,"h":24}," Bat Dragons to spawn in specific stages."]}],"infobox":[{"title":"Relic","rows":[{"label":"Release","cells":[["6 June 2026 (Update)"]]},{"label":"ID","cells":[["RELIC_GREENEYES"]]},{"label":"Effects","cells":[["Allows Bat Dragons to be found in ",{"t":"Il Molise","r":"stage:il-molise"}," and ",{"t":"Mad Forest","r":"stage:mad-forest"},"."]]},{"label":"Location","cells":[[{"t":"The Lycaeum","r":"stage:the-lycaeum"}]]}]}],"sections":[{"id":"obtaining","title":"Obtaining","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["Green Eyes Vizard is found by purchasing it with ",{"i":"Sprite-Gold_Coin.png","w":10,"h":10}," 60,000 from ",{"i":"Sprite-Big_Troubler.png","w":22,"h":24}," Big Troubler in ",{"t":"The Lycaeum","r":"stage:the-lycaeum"},". Once Green Eyes Vizard has been purchased, it cannot be purchased again."]},{"k":"p","c":["Alternatively, the Green Eyes Vizard can be unlocked in ",{"i":"Sprite-Forbidden_Scrolls_of_Morbane.png","w":16,"h":16,"r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," ",{"t":"Forbidden Scrolls of Morbane","r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," by casting the spell \"greeneyesbatdragon\"."]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"update-history","title":"Update history","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["This information has been manually compiled. Some updates may not be included yet."]},{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["update ",{"i":"Steam_logo.svg","w":16,"h":16,"a":"Steam"}," 6 June 2026 (Update):"],"sub":{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Added to game."]}]}}]},{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["beta ",{"i":"Steam_logo.svg","w":16,"h":16,"a":"Steam"}," 1 April 2026 (Update):"],"sub":{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Released in beta version."]}]}}]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"trivia","title":"Trivia","blocks":[{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["The spell \"greeneyesbatdragon\" references the animated series and trading card game ",{"t":"Yu-Gi-Oh!","x":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu-Gi-Oh!"},", specifically the iconic ",{"t":"Blue-Eyes White Dragon","x":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Blue-Eyes_White_Dragon"}," and ",{"t":"Red-Eyes Black Dragon","x":"https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Red-Eyes_Black_Dragon"},"."]},{"c":["The spell's name also references the 1986 film ",{"t":"Big Trouble in Little China","x":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Trouble_in_Little_China"},", in which the main antagonist, David Lo Pan, seeks to marry a woman with green eyes and sacrifice her to the god Ching Dai in order to gain immortality."]}]}],"subs":[]}]}